+## Mathematical verification and dependency consequences
+
+**E0, line by line.** The inherited definition in W3-POST/STATEMENT.md:36-38 minimizes over m>=s0 and imposes R_m<=n^(-(s0+2)/2). The source [T03R] PROOF.md:22 gives q_(m+1)/w(s0)=C(p,s0) product_{i=s0}^m rho_i. For m<min(B,K), q_(m+1) is present in R_m. Every denominator 2p-1-i is positive. If p>=2B, i<B implies rho_i>=(p-B)/(2p)>=1/4; otherwise rho_i>=1/(2p)>=1/(4B). There are m-s0+1<=B factors, each at least 1/(4B), and C(p,s0)>=1. Thus R_m>=(4B)^(-B), uniformly in p. Choosing n0 strictly above (4B)^(2B/(s0+2)) excludes every candidate m below min(B,K). If K<B this excludes all m<K and the admissible endpoint is K, where R_K=0. This is valid in the ticket's R1 domain s0<=K. E1 uses B=j0; D3 uses B=s0+j0; both are fixed functions of s0,A, so no new n0 dependence leaks into the stated rates. E2 and C case (iii) consume E1 and need no further hypothesis changes.
+
+**Intercept, line by line.** By the truth convention in W3-POST/STATEMENT.md:31, ybar^r=alpha*+mean(X^r beta*)+epsilonbar, while mu=CX^r beta*. Consequently the raw fitted-minus-true mean is epsilonbar 1+(muhat-mu). Both fitted and true centered means lie in 1-perp. Squaring gives exactly n epsilonbar^2+||muhat-mu||^2. Repeating D0:12-17 yields the displayed Hellinger upper bound, and Gaussian noise gives n epsilonbar^2/sigma*^2~chi-square_1. For D(a), n h_int^2 is posterior-tight in sampling probability, hence every diverging M_n threshold works. For D(b), one must use slack rather than simply append a positive term to an exhausted bound: apply the uniform variance result D3:70-72 with M_n=sqrt(log n/2). Its squared contribution is <=(log n)/(2n) outside vanishing posterior mass; epsilonbar^2/(4sigma*^2)=o_P(log n/n), so it fits inside the remaining (log n)/(2n). Thus exactly C_H_prime=1+C_H/(4sigma*^2) still works. STATEMENT and REPORT carry this extension; no coefficient or selection premise changes.
+
+**Exact B implication.** The constant comparison requires the existing refined exact-reference proof at B:45-48; inserting B into the generic display alone would retain an unnecessary sqrt(B) term. With r=0 that term vanishes. The resulting constant 1/sqrt(2)+1/2+[M+M/(2phi0^2)]/(2sigma*^2) is <= W3-POST Lemma 1a's C_Lambda at STATEMENT.md:48, because that original constant has the additional positive sigma*^2 contribution. The determinant normalization transfers the same tail inequality. The stronger relation in the statement, report table and registry is therefore supported.
+
+**P1 - false propagated cutoff chain (required repair).** At D_hellinger.md:53 the error is the comparison between the numerical upper bound s0+j0-1 and K, not E0. For a concrete admissible sequence take p=2, s0=A=1, centered orthogonal standardized columns, and a bounded nonzero truth coefficient. F0, E and OS hold, and K=2 for every n>=4. Underfitting models (including the empty model) exist. Nevertheless the printed middle inequality reads 4<=2. Replace that portion by
+
+`|S| <= min(s0+j0-1,K) <= min(s0+j0,K) <= m_sharp_n`.
+
+This follows by combining |S|-s0+j0-1 with S in Omega, rather than asserting the first bound itself is <=K. E0 then proves the final step. The intended D(b) theorem is repairable without changing constants or premises. As requested, this review does not repair the proof file. D(b)'s report/registry and intercept extension inherit reliance on a proof containing this false line.
+
+**P2 - N2 qualification not propagated everywhere.** C1A finding 2 explicitly linked its concern to A_occam.md:33. That line still says OS "allows, at fixed p, e.g. an exactly duplicated null pair (numerics N2)"; ASSUMPTION_MAP.md:14 still says ADG is "improvable to (OS) (N2)." These present a stronger asymptotic example claim than REPORT.md:149-150 and :193, which explicitly say no asymptotic proof for this example is given. This is not a counterexample to OS or A0; it is an incomplete propagation of the evidential downgrade. Add the same finite-n qualification or supply the missing explicit asymptotic argument. The disposition's "all findings applied" is too broad on this point.
+
+**P3 - predictive sharpness qualification not uniform.** REPORT.md:161 now says the 1/n scale is argued, not proved as a lower bound. ASSUMPTION_MAP.md:59 still asserts it "cannot be improved," and D_hellinger.md:95-96 pairs a no-lower-bound header with that assertion. The conditional-spread argument may support the assertion, but no new formal lower-bound proof was added. These summaries should use the report's proof-status qualification. This does not negate D(a)'s upper rate.
+
+There is no evidence of a new post-council adoption of C+, D+, or E's ridge hypothesis: both C1 seats explicitly audited them. The actual new analytic work is E0 and the intercept extension; the strengthened B relation relies on an existing refined proof. No later LOG entry supplies a re-check of the added D3 chain.
